1
00:00:04,813 --> 00:00:05,553
[SPEAKER_00]: So, what's jhāna?

2
00:00:28,466 --> 00:00:30,287
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, people think jhāna is something you can enter.

3
00:00:31,908 --> 00:00:32,228
[SPEAKER_00]: Hmm.

4
00:00:33,789 --> 00:00:34,629
[SPEAKER_01]: You can't enter jhāna.

5
00:00:37,247 --> 00:00:38,467
[SPEAKER_01]: Jhāna enters you, basically.

6
00:00:41,088 --> 00:00:41,888
[SPEAKER_01]: Jhāna is the result.

7
00:00:44,408 --> 00:00:45,208
[SPEAKER_01]: A mode of being.

8
00:00:47,189 --> 00:00:47,509
[SPEAKER_01]: Okay.

9
00:00:49,289 --> 00:00:49,989
[SPEAKER_01]: It's the result.

10
00:00:50,829 --> 00:00:52,290
[SPEAKER_00]: It's the consequence.

11
00:00:52,850 --> 00:00:53,030
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

12
00:00:53,930 --> 00:00:54,090
[SPEAKER_01]: Of.

13
00:00:55,110 --> 00:00:55,750
[SPEAKER_01]: We'll get to that.

14
00:00:57,991 --> 00:01:00,851
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why we said there is no I am in jhāna.

15
00:01:01,431 --> 00:01:04,452
[SPEAKER_01]: You can't say I am in jhāna, I'm entering jhāna, I was in jhāna.

16
00:01:07,051 --> 00:01:07,591
[SPEAKER_01]: It subsides.

17
00:01:07,711 --> 00:01:14,374
[SPEAKER_01]: For as long as you think jhāna is something you can enter, literally, something waiting for you to enter it, that's not jhāna.

18
00:01:14,594 --> 00:01:14,814
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

19
00:01:15,534 --> 00:01:27,780
[SPEAKER_00]: So, is it worth saying that in the... often in the translations of the jhānas, it says that one enters upon and dwells in jhāna.

20
00:01:28,360 --> 00:01:28,840
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's wrong.

21
00:01:28,940 --> 00:01:29,280
[SPEAKER_01]: That's wrong.

22
00:01:29,300 --> 00:01:30,601
[SPEAKER_00]: It doesn't say that in Pāli.

23
00:01:31,161 --> 00:01:34,182
[SPEAKER_00]: No, it says one dwells in jhāna, having acquired it.

24
00:01:34,242 --> 00:01:35,943
[SPEAKER_00]: Having upāsāṃpajñā, whatever.

25
00:01:35,963 --> 00:01:36,143
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

26
00:01:36,627 --> 00:01:40,908
[SPEAKER_00]: Whatever... even entity, if you want to translate it like that, but the point is...

27
00:01:40,928 --> 00:01:42,188
[SPEAKER_00]: It's something that's already happened.

28
00:01:42,208 --> 00:01:48,109
[SPEAKER_00]: Based on the consequence of jhāna, of your mode of being, now, you know you acquired it.

29
00:01:49,050 --> 00:01:49,790
[SPEAKER_00]: Not the other way around.

30
00:01:49,830 --> 00:01:52,950
[SPEAKER_01]: I acquired it and thus I entered it and then that's how I dwell in it.

31
00:01:53,551 --> 00:01:55,071
[SPEAKER_01]: Which is usually the perception of it.

32
00:01:55,691 --> 00:02:03,613
[SPEAKER_01]: Meditation technique, object, having an overwhelming experience, surge of pleasure or whatever, or I enter jhāna, now I am in the jhāna.

33
00:02:03,873 --> 00:02:04,833
[SPEAKER_01]: It's completely wrong order.

34
00:02:06,529 --> 00:02:10,551
[SPEAKER_01]: So, when I say jhāna enters you, it's more accurate to regard it like that.

35
00:02:10,851 --> 00:02:21,596
[SPEAKER_01]: It's basically, as I said, mode of being or even becomes your point of view, your new point of view, point of view that doesn't see I am as first.

36
00:02:25,358 --> 00:02:31,321
[SPEAKER_00]: So, it's... it's a point of view that's... that involves a different order.

37
00:02:31,701 --> 00:02:33,322
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes, and that's a... that's a result.

38
00:02:34,327 --> 00:02:41,132
[SPEAKER_01]: of certain contemplations, certain understanding, certain development of the mind.

39
00:02:43,774 --> 00:02:52,380
[SPEAKER_01]: And, eh... if you wonder which type of development of the mind, just read literally any jhāna description.

40
00:02:52,400 --> 00:02:53,901
[SPEAKER_00]: It says it clear as a day.

41
00:02:54,381 --> 00:02:58,924
[SPEAKER_00]: So, at the top of my head, quite secluded from... Seclusion from sensuality.

42
00:02:59,985 --> 00:03:02,707
[SPEAKER_01]: There is absolutely no description of the first jhāna

43
00:03:03,519 --> 00:03:04,640
[SPEAKER_01]: That does not say that.

44
00:03:05,300 --> 00:03:08,543
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, that that's just one way you can enter it.

45
00:03:08,623 --> 00:03:08,863
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

46
00:03:09,104 --> 00:03:09,264
[SPEAKER_00]: No.

47
00:03:10,044 --> 00:03:11,606
[SPEAKER_01]: It's always.

48
00:03:11,666 --> 00:03:15,709
[SPEAKER_01]: Jhāna is the result of your seclusion.

49
00:03:17,050 --> 00:03:19,232
[SPEAKER_01]: Seclusion is not because of your jhāna.

50
00:03:19,352 --> 00:03:20,433
[SPEAKER_01]: Jhāna is because seclusion.

51
00:03:21,274 --> 00:03:24,516
[SPEAKER_01]: And if you have any doubt about that, it's in the within the same description.

52
00:03:24,536 --> 00:03:24,977
[SPEAKER_01]: It is, yeah.

53
00:03:24,997 --> 00:03:25,517
[SPEAKER_01]: The pleasure.

54
00:03:25,717 --> 00:03:25,917
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

55
00:03:26,338 --> 00:03:28,940
[SPEAKER_01]: The pleasure of the first jhāna is not of the first jhāna.

56
00:03:29,360 --> 00:03:31,202
[SPEAKER_01]: The pleasure is of the seclusion.

57
00:03:31,906 --> 00:03:51,341
[SPEAKER_00]: Viveka jhāna, so pīti-sukhaṅga-viveka jhāna, so it's the bliss and joy and happiness born of the seclusion from sense-desire or sensuality and other wholesome states which pertains to any kind of bodily hindrances of any kind.

58
00:03:52,162 --> 00:03:56,205
[SPEAKER_01]: But the common notion is, I enter jhāna, then I feel pleasure.

59
00:03:58,427 --> 00:03:58,587
[SPEAKER_01]: No.

60
00:03:59,207 --> 00:04:00,188
[SPEAKER_01]: Pleasure comes first.

61
00:04:00,782 --> 00:04:04,267
[SPEAKER_01]: Not pleasure of jhāna, but pleasure of seclusion, which is what jhāna is.

62
00:04:05,428 --> 00:04:08,452
[SPEAKER_01]: Which is, at the time, that's what your point of view becomes.

63
00:04:08,613 --> 00:04:09,654
[SPEAKER_01]: That's what your being is.

64
00:04:10,495 --> 00:04:15,322
[SPEAKER_01]: There is no room for I am experiencing this pleasure, I am entering, I am exiting this jhāna and what not.

65
00:04:18,964 --> 00:04:27,810
[SPEAKER_01]: So, I mean, very clear, partly, yet the entire contemporary notions are about watching your nostrils, having the ecstatic experience...

66
00:04:28,010 --> 00:04:28,651
[SPEAKER_00]: Stopping thinking.

67
00:04:28,971 --> 00:04:34,055
[SPEAKER_01]: Stop your thinking, of course, and then you have this surge of pleasure and there must have been jhāna there.

68
00:04:34,635 --> 00:04:49,086
[SPEAKER_00]: So, the standard idea of jhāna being absorption, involving not thinking, you know, you can't have the idea of thinking with jhāna, and yet these words vittaka-vicāra appear.

69
00:04:49,166 --> 00:04:51,108
[SPEAKER_01]: Are the main characteristic of the first jhāna.

70
00:04:51,128 --> 00:04:58,073
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you get these strange translations of... it's not really thinking, it's like a sustained thought and applied...

71
00:04:58,193 --> 00:04:59,054
[SPEAKER_00]: It's literally thinking.

72
00:04:59,094 --> 00:05:02,737
[SPEAKER_01]: Vittaka-vicāra always go together as well, and it literally is just...

73
00:05:03,918 --> 00:05:05,159
[SPEAKER_01]: Amplifying the same.

74
00:05:05,839 --> 00:05:10,982
[SPEAKER_01]: With thinking, with pondering, with things going on in his mind, that's the first jhāna.

75
00:05:11,402 --> 00:05:16,826
[SPEAKER_01]: It doesn't say, oh, with thinking, the first factor, with pondering, with the second factor.

76
00:05:18,246 --> 00:05:23,970
[SPEAKER_01]: Nor is it, yeah, applied and sustained thought and in some sort of concocted method that you do.

77
00:05:24,370 --> 00:05:26,091
[SPEAKER_01]: No, it's with thinking and with pondering.

78
00:05:26,352 --> 00:05:26,532
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

79
00:05:26,772 --> 00:05:29,174
[SPEAKER_01]: Just with, with wandering, with roaming about.

80
00:05:29,355 --> 00:05:29,575
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

81
00:05:29,595 --> 00:05:30,796
[SPEAKER_00]: So, they're not really different things.

82
00:05:31,316 --> 00:05:31,717
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

83
00:05:31,797 --> 00:05:32,157
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

84
00:05:32,197 --> 00:05:35,039
[SPEAKER_01]: Just slightly two different aspects, I suppose.

85
00:05:35,059 --> 00:05:35,239
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

86
00:05:35,500 --> 00:05:38,702
[SPEAKER_01]: Of your thinking, which are kind of in separate, practically speaking.

87
00:05:38,722 --> 00:05:41,425
[SPEAKER_00]: Near synonyms to talk about, maybe, different extents.

88
00:05:41,705 --> 00:05:42,145
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

89
00:05:42,185 --> 00:05:42,646
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

90
00:05:42,666 --> 00:05:44,667
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

91
00:05:48,951 --> 00:05:49,131
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

92
00:05:49,151 --> 00:05:53,595
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that, well, that's another extremely gratuitous notion of my thinking will stop in the first jhāna.

93
00:05:54,905 --> 00:05:57,407
[SPEAKER_01]: I had this experience where I was not aware of myself.

94
00:05:57,627 --> 00:05:58,588
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, not just thinking.

95
00:05:58,888 --> 00:05:59,829
[SPEAKER_01]: All the senses stopped.

96
00:05:59,849 --> 00:06:01,550
[SPEAKER_01]: Of anything, yeah.

97
00:06:01,610 --> 00:06:07,535
[SPEAKER_01]: Yet, in Mahajanma 111, every single jhāna has this absolute clarity of mindfulness as its basis.

98
00:06:07,795 --> 00:06:08,076
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

99
00:06:08,756 --> 00:06:10,958
[SPEAKER_00]: And brings mindfulness to the fulfillment.

100
00:06:10,978 --> 00:06:13,520
[SPEAKER_00]: This phenomenon, this phenomenon, seeing all of these things.

101
00:06:13,600 --> 00:06:14,020
[SPEAKER_00]: Exactly.

102
00:06:14,040 --> 00:06:14,421
[SPEAKER_00]: Exactly.

103
00:06:14,441 --> 00:06:15,962
[SPEAKER_00]: See what's there.

104
00:06:16,022 --> 00:06:19,645
[SPEAKER_01]: So, basically, it's imperturbable mindfulness, not the absence of it.

105
00:06:23,148 --> 00:06:24,549
[SPEAKER_01]: So, how you want to develop first jhāna?

106
00:06:25,755 --> 00:06:27,136
[SPEAKER_01]: Seclude yourself from centrality.

107
00:06:28,736 --> 00:06:30,397
[SPEAKER_01]: How can you seclude yourself from centrality?

108
00:06:31,017 --> 00:06:32,538
[SPEAKER_01]: By understanding the extent of it.

109
00:06:33,878 --> 00:06:36,440
[SPEAKER_01]: The extent of your involvement, the extent of your engagement.

110
00:06:37,180 --> 00:06:40,041
[SPEAKER_01]: The basis, the necessary basis for your engagement with centrality.

111
00:06:40,481 --> 00:06:41,962
[SPEAKER_01]: You understand that, you surmount it.

112
00:06:44,543 --> 00:06:46,904
[SPEAKER_01]: Having surmounted it, you will know that you surmounted it.

113
00:06:47,504 --> 00:06:51,846
[SPEAKER_01]: And then that pleasure of relief, which is a pleasure of the first jhāna, it will be felt.

114
00:06:52,306 --> 00:06:53,767
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's what the first jhāna is.

115
00:06:55,196 --> 00:06:58,398
[SPEAKER_01]: The result of that development, basically.

116
00:07:00,059 --> 00:07:19,590
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you could see how, like, even back in the day, jhāna, as we discussed before, even in in old Vedas and stuff, meant contemplation, investigating even, thinking over, pondering over something, like either virtues of a deity that you want to develop in yourself, or anything else.

117
00:07:19,610 --> 00:07:20,431
[SPEAKER_01]: But the point was,

118
00:07:21,518 --> 00:07:23,581
[SPEAKER_01]: You dwell on it, in order to develop it.

119
00:07:23,601 --> 00:07:24,342
[SPEAKER_01]: Do you think about it?

120
00:07:24,582 --> 00:07:24,762
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

121
00:07:24,862 --> 00:07:27,446
[SPEAKER_01]: You're not like trying to negate the whole idea of thinking.

122
00:07:27,606 --> 00:07:27,886
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

123
00:07:28,968 --> 00:07:31,852
[SPEAKER_01]: If you want to surmount your thinking, that's the second jhāna.

124
00:07:32,933 --> 00:07:36,698
[SPEAKER_01]: And you can't surmount the second... your thinking if you haven't even developed it properly.

125
00:07:36,718 --> 00:07:36,898
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

126
00:07:37,940 --> 00:07:39,502
[SPEAKER_01]: If all you do is go around denying it.

127
00:07:50,788 --> 00:07:54,490
[SPEAKER_00]: So, but jhānas involve a particular theme.

128
00:07:55,150 --> 00:07:55,370
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

129
00:07:56,871 --> 00:08:01,253
[SPEAKER_01]: We think of jhānas as particularly directed mindfulness.

130
00:08:02,794 --> 00:08:09,577
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why in all those other, in some other suttas, it's like, you can develop jhāna on the basis of mindfulness of the corpse.

131
00:08:10,097 --> 00:08:10,317
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

132
00:08:10,617 --> 00:08:19,802
[SPEAKER_01]: We develop jhāna on the basis of mindfulness of the charnel ground, or the, I don't know, discussing the senses, or mindfulness of breathing, or body postures.

133
00:08:21,660 --> 00:08:23,201
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's not... it's not an automatic method.

134
00:08:23,221 --> 00:08:26,682
[SPEAKER_01]: It's just a way of regarding things on the basis of mindfulness.

135
00:08:26,722 --> 00:08:27,502
[SPEAKER_00]: On the basis of mindfulness.

136
00:08:28,863 --> 00:08:29,643
[SPEAKER_01]: Way of regarding what?

137
00:08:30,003 --> 00:08:31,724
[SPEAKER_00]: Sensuality.

138
00:08:31,744 --> 00:08:36,506
[SPEAKER_01]: Way of regarding sensuality whereby you remind yourself the extent of it that you know you're free from.

139
00:08:37,506 --> 00:08:39,967
[SPEAKER_01]: Dwelling that, that is the bliss of the first jhāna.

140
00:08:42,628 --> 00:08:43,068
[SPEAKER_01]: That is...

141
00:08:43,088 --> 00:08:50,611
[SPEAKER_01]: So, as I said, like the... the first jhāna is not developed by magically entering it and then having pleasure from it.

142
00:08:51,208 --> 00:09:01,619
[SPEAKER_01]: The actual technique, the practice of meditation of the first jhāna, is the practice of understanding the central extent, the extent of unwholesome.

143
00:09:02,540 --> 00:09:04,302
[SPEAKER_01]: That is your practice of first jhāna.

144
00:09:07,918 --> 00:09:13,421
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why it's impossible to engage in sensuality on the level... on the basis of first jhāna.

145
00:09:13,441 --> 00:09:25,907
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why the one with the right view, on the basis of first jhāna, would be free from sensuality, even when he's not anymore in the first jhāna, because he would have seen this... he would have been seeing clearly its nature of... of actually being repulsive.

146
00:09:27,448 --> 00:09:35,072
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's just to basically convict the idea that you can not be celibate and not keep the precepts and have... and enter jhānas.

147
00:09:36,473 --> 00:09:36,933
[SPEAKER_01]: Impossible.

148
00:09:38,175 --> 00:09:44,677
[SPEAKER_01]: On a necessary basis, for the consequence of jhāna, first jhāna, is quite secluded from sensual pleasures.

149
00:09:45,017 --> 00:09:46,658
[SPEAKER_01]: Quite removed, basically.

150
00:09:47,358 --> 00:09:48,238
[SPEAKER_01]: Separated from.

151
00:09:48,258 --> 00:09:51,580
[SPEAKER_01]: Quite as in very, as in, as in, basically, yeah, yeah, yeah.

152
00:09:51,780 --> 00:09:52,820
[SPEAKER_01]: Quite as in indeed.

153
00:09:53,340 --> 00:09:54,801
[SPEAKER_01]: Indeed, he's separate from it.

154
00:09:54,821 --> 00:09:55,041
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

155
00:09:55,861 --> 00:09:56,821
[SPEAKER_01]: And he's developed that.

156
00:09:56,861 --> 00:09:58,082
[SPEAKER_01]: He's, every time.

157
00:09:58,122 --> 00:10:00,263
[SPEAKER_01]: Separate from, from sensual states.

158
00:10:00,343 --> 00:10:01,783
[SPEAKER_01]: Separate from unwholesome states.

159
00:10:03,264 --> 00:10:06,605
[SPEAKER_01]: Pleasure arises as a result of the recognition of that.

160
00:10:08,067 --> 00:10:09,628
[SPEAKER_01]: He cultivates that very thing.

161
00:10:11,008 --> 00:10:13,249
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's how he abides in the first jhāna.

162
00:10:13,609 --> 00:10:14,389
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's what Buddha said.

163
00:10:15,810 --> 00:10:18,011
[SPEAKER_01]: He would dwell in the first jhāna, having acquired it.

164
00:10:19,071 --> 00:10:28,434
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, whether he sits, walks, extends his arms, goes to the toilet, whatever he does while he dwells in the first jhāna, it's divine, because his mind is in the first jhāna.

165
00:10:28,474 --> 00:10:28,654
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

166
00:10:30,655 --> 00:10:33,036
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's what vihārata means, dwelling.

167
00:10:33,792 --> 00:10:36,012
[SPEAKER_01]: It doesn't mean temporarily overwhelmed by something.

168
00:10:36,152 --> 00:10:37,913
[SPEAKER_01]: It means literally you're dwelling.

169
00:10:37,933 --> 00:10:42,954
[SPEAKER_01]: So, while you're dwelling in this kuti, you eat, you drink, you lay down, you sit.

170
00:10:43,274 --> 00:10:44,994
[SPEAKER_01]: You're doing these things while you're dwelling in it.

171
00:10:46,075 --> 00:10:48,295
[SPEAKER_01]: Hence the same principle of the jhāna.

172
00:10:58,137 --> 00:10:59,137
[SPEAKER_01]: So, more specifically,

173
00:11:03,559 --> 00:11:26,566
[SPEAKER_01]: Practicing that... well, practicing the first jhāna, which means practicing with separation from unwholesome states and sensuality, is done not by chasing down the sensual states, but by seeing a common basis to all unwholesome states, to all five entrances.

174
00:11:27,227 --> 00:11:31,108
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why the five entrances are the five that are abandoned in the first jhāna.

175
00:11:33,417 --> 00:11:41,982
[SPEAKER_01]: Sensuality, ill-will, restlessness, laziness, distraction, doubt.

176
00:11:42,282 --> 00:11:43,943
[SPEAKER_01]: What all of those things have in common?

177
00:11:45,925 --> 00:11:48,566
[SPEAKER_01]: What is the necessary basis, necessary container?

178
00:11:53,209 --> 00:11:53,489
[SPEAKER_01]: Body.

179
00:11:54,210 --> 00:11:54,470
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

180
00:11:56,751 --> 00:11:57,552
[SPEAKER_01]: Body being there.

181
00:11:59,273 --> 00:12:02,535
[SPEAKER_01]: And see, even when people were to engage with them,

182
00:12:03,165 --> 00:12:07,289
[SPEAKER_01]: Say, you were overwhelmed by hindrance and you give in to sensuality or expression of will or whatever.

183
00:12:07,789 --> 00:12:09,711
[SPEAKER_01]: You're not really leaving the body.

184
00:12:10,051 --> 00:12:11,633
[SPEAKER_01]: You can't, even if you want to.

185
00:12:11,753 --> 00:12:14,455
[SPEAKER_01]: You're not actually going further into these things.

186
00:12:14,816 --> 00:12:21,322
[SPEAKER_01]: You're just basically increasing their density, so to speak, density of their significance, within the same basis.

187
00:12:23,244 --> 00:12:25,286
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why anger is felt bodily.

188
00:12:25,326 --> 00:12:26,627
[SPEAKER_01]: Sensuality is felt bodily.

189
00:12:26,727 --> 00:12:27,788
[SPEAKER_01]: Doubt is felt bodily.

190
00:12:28,618 --> 00:12:36,083
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, that's so... some people... that's not so obvious, that doubt is... Yeah, but how... like, how do you know that doubt is unpleasant?

191
00:12:36,383 --> 00:12:36,763
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, exactly.

192
00:12:36,783 --> 00:12:38,344
[SPEAKER_01]: Because you feel it unpleasantly.

193
00:12:38,384 --> 00:12:39,225
[SPEAKER_01]: Your body is a fake.

194
00:12:39,245 --> 00:12:40,165
[SPEAKER_01]: You can't sleep at night.

195
00:12:40,185 --> 00:12:42,227
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

196
